(66, 76, '* { box-sizing: border-box; } body {margin: 0;}*{box-sizing:border-box;}body{margin:0;}#ioxk1{font-size:18px;color:black;}', '&lt;div class=&quot;site-wrapper-reveal&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;about-banner-wrap banner-space about-us-bg&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-8 m-auto&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;about-banner-content text-center&quot;&gt;&lt;h1 id=&quot;i67r&quot; class=&quot;mb-15 text-white&quot;&gt;Blog&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!--===========  feature-large-images-wrapper  Start =============--&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;ivjxw&quot; class=&quot;feature-large-images-wrapper section-space--ptb_100&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-12&quot;&gt;&lt;!-- section-title-wrap Start --&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;section-title-wrap text-center section-space--mb_60&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://5.imimg.com/data5/SELLER/Default/2023/2/UU/PR/OP/8000916/dmit-dermatoglyphics-multiple-intelligence-test--500x500.png&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; id=&quot;idiufj&quot; class=&quot;img-fluid&quot;/&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;ioxk1&quot; class=&quot;text&quot;&gt;Once a student reaches the 9th and the 10th grade, one of the most prominent questions he or she faces is which stream will choose after her schooling? The questions are numerous and the answers are equally confusing! Reason?&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;There are various suggestions from parents, peer pressures, suggestions from relatives, neighbours, and so on… In such a scenario, how then the confused teenager would be able to take decisions on the right stream for him/her and subsequently the right career path?&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;While it certainly can be overwhelming and puzzling for one to decide on the right career path, there is a scientific analysis that can be studied for the same reason in accurately deciding a career. A psychometric test is one of the perfect ways to understand the type of career a person wishes to have.&lt;br/&gt;Before that, we take a look at the different types of intelligence and how one can use them for their benefit to decide on the right career in life.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;According to the renowned American psychologist, Howard Gardner, all human beings possess 8 different types of intelligence-&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Naturalist Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Naturalist intelligence is one having a deep understanding of all things natural. These people incline toward nature and are interested in reading about nature, geography, topography, climate, etc. Such people can be good horticulturalists, landscape artists, scientists, farmers, biologists, etc.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Linguistic Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Have you ever heard anyone say, she is good in languages but is not able to score well in Math’s! Such a person possesses linguistic intelligence or commands over the language. Their strengths are writing, words, and language. Communication comes very easily to them and they are extremely confident. Such people can be teachers, translators, writers, interpreters, journalists, lawyers, poets, script writers, or speech therapists.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Logical and Mathematical Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Some people are experts at solving mathematical problems at the drop of a hat. They also have a knack for solving complex puzzles, and logical word problems or are swift calculators. Such people possess an inclination towards logical or mathematical intelligence. Careers suitable for such people are those mathematicians, engineers, accountants, computer programmers, scientists, bankers, auditors, chartered accountants, etc.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Musical Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;People with musical intelligence show a liking for music, arts, and culture from a very young age. They like listening to different music, catching rhythms easily, thinking about sounds and patterns, and having a unique understanding of music and patterns. Such people can be good musicians, singers, background musicians, instrument-playing artists, composers, music teachers, and music arrangers.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Spatial Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Spatial intelligence refers to a kind of intelligence in which a person has a liking for drawing, and arranging shapes, is good at solving visual puzzles, and interprets patterns. Careers suitable for this intelligence are architects, interior designers, landscape designers, visual artists, graphic designers, animators, cartoonists, and industrial designers.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Bodily-Kinesthetic Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Is your child good at gymnastics, does he or she prefers sports over any other activity? Is he or she great at bodily movements and motor control skills? Then probably you should go for a career which will shape you’re these very skills. Careers suitable for these are actors, choreographers, sportsmen, sports teachers, sports psychologists, and firefighters.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Intrapersonal Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Some people are great at solving problems alone, work to the best of their ability in isolation, and are happy being their boss. Careers suitable for such people are entrepreneurs, psychologists, therapists, authors, writers, and researchers.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Interpersonal Intelligence&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/b&gt;Some people have an amazing ability to understand people, and their emotions, create healthy relationships and show a capability to solve complex problems between people. Careers suitable for such people are teachers, professors, HR managers, sales managers, politicians, managers, school principals, public relations officers, administrators, and nurses.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;A person has all of the above 8 intelligences, however, they differ in their impact. Some have more interpersonal intelligence, other has kinesthetic intelligence, some show an interest in interacting with peoples more, and others prefer working in isolation.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;How then are we to find out which is the ideal career path for aspiring teenagers. DMIT counseling for students is one of the proven techniques to help choose students on their ideal career path.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;At DMIT our team will guide you in choosing the right career path to embark on your journey to success.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- section-title-wrap Start --&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!--===========  feature-large-images-wrapper  End =============--&gt;&lt;!--========= About Resources Wrapper Start ===========--&gt;&lt;!--========= About Resources Wrapper End ===========--&gt;&lt;!--========= About Delivering Wrapper Start ===========--&gt;&lt;!--=========== fun fact Wrapper Start ==========--&gt;&lt;!--=========== fun fact Wrapper End ==========--&gt;&lt;!--====================  testimonial section ====================--&gt;&lt;!--====================  End of testimonial section  ====================--&gt;&lt;!--====================  brand logo slider area ====================--&gt;&lt;!--====================  End of brand logo slider area  ====================--&gt;&lt;!--============ Contact Us Area Start =================--&gt;&lt;!--============ Contact Us Area End =================--&gt;&lt;/div&gt;', 15, '1', '2024-09-03 08:25:46', '2024-09-07 10:44:01');
